
  Welcome to GeSI — the guided Gentoo installer (CLI).

  This is the barebones console installer image. It boots straight into GeST's
  "Install Gentoo" TUI: a guided, step-by-step install (partition a disk, unpack
  a stage3, build a kernel, install a bootloader) — the Gentoo Handbook, driven
  by GeST, YaST-style, from the console.

  If you exit the installer you land here, at a root shell (no password on the
  live medium). Re-run it any time with:  gest --install

  Networking: a wired link usually comes up via DHCP automatically. For Wi-Fi,
  run `wpa_supplicant`/`iw` by hand, or use GeST → Network → Wi-Fi, before
  installing (the install downloads a stage3 and emerges packages).

  Tip: this image installs a base Gentoo system. To get a full HeDE desktop,
  turn on the desktop option in GeST's installer.
